# Conflict fixture: a catch-all rule followed by a more-specific rule that
# assigns different owners, leaving a deliberate coverage gap for generated
# files (no-owner pattern via a rule with no owners is not supported by GitHub
# CODEOWNERS — an empty-owner line is simply skipped by the parser).
#
# Pattern precedence (GitHub semantics): LAST matching rule wins.
#
# For `src/generated/schema.ts`:
#   1. `**/*.ts`      matches → owners: @typescript-guild     (overridden)
#   2. `src/generated/**` matches → owners: @tooling-team     ← WINS
#
# For `src/codeowners.ts`:
#   1. `**/*.ts`      matches → owners: @typescript-guild     ← WINS
#   (rule 2 does not match)
#
# For `scripts/build.sh`:
#   No rule matches → uncovered

**/*.ts           @typescript-guild
src/generated/**  @tooling-team
